1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,610
At six-oh-two in the morning my phone made a sound I had never heard before.

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:06,197
Not a ringtone.

3
00:00:06,547 --> 00:00:07,562
An alarm.

4
00:00:08,462 --> 00:00:10,767
The screen said: emergency alert.

5
00:00:11,117 --> 00:00:12,353
Remain calm.

6
00:00:12,703 --> 00:00:14,956
Next update in twenty-four hours.

7
00:00:15,856 --> 00:00:17,731
I read the last line twice.

8
00:00:18,081 --> 00:00:19,526
Twenty-four hours.

9
00:00:19,876 --> 00:00:23,469
Whoever wrote it did not think I would need to know anything sooner.

10
00:00:24,369 --> 00:00:25,788
I called my sister.

11
00:00:26,138 --> 00:00:27,492
It rang and rang.

12
00:00:27,842 --> 00:00:29,743
I called a friend across town.

13
00:00:30,093 --> 00:00:30,913
Nothing.

14
00:00:31,263 --> 00:00:35,638
I called the emergency number, and a recording told me that all lines were busy.

15
00:00:35,988 --> 00:00:40,024
Eight percent of my battery, gone, and I knew nothing more than before.

16
00:00:40,924 --> 00:00:42,408
I walked to the window.

17
00:00:42,758 --> 00:00:47,055
Down on the street, a man ran past a stopped car with his shoes in his hand.

18
00:00:47,405 --> 00:00:49,371
A woman was screaming a name.

19
00:00:49,721 --> 00:00:53,588
Someone was leaning on a horn, and nobody was telling him to stop.

20
00:00:53,938 --> 00:01:00,539
At the far end of the block, a few people were walking toward the crowd, slowly, in a way that made the crowd run faster.

21
00:01:01,439 --> 00:01:03,926
I did not understand what I was looking at.

22
00:01:04,276 --> 00:01:09,744
I understood only one thing: everyone was running, and I did not want to be the one who stayed behind.

23
00:01:10,645 --> 00:01:12,910
I packed in a hurry, without thinking.

24
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:14,835
Two bottles of water.

25
00:01:15,185 --> 00:01:16,552
Two snack bars.

26
00:01:16,902 --> 00:01:19,298
My flashlight, because it was by the bed.

27
00:01:19,648 --> 00:01:22,135
My phone, at seventy-seven percent.

28
00:01:22,485 --> 00:01:27,302
I grabbed the small backpack from the hook by the door, and I left the door open behind me.

29
00:01:28,202 --> 00:01:30,572
That was the first decision of the day.

30
00:01:30,922 --> 00:01:34,398
I would make many more before night, and most of them would be wrong.

31
00:01:35,298 --> 00:01:39,308
Everyone on the street was running the same way, so I ran the same way.

32
00:01:39,658 --> 00:01:40,804
Toward the mall.

33
00:01:41,704 --> 00:01:44,946
It had big doors, bright lights, security guards.

34
00:01:45,296 --> 00:01:47,913
It looked like the kind of place that would be safe.

35
00:01:48,263 --> 00:01:52,455
It did not occur to me that this was exactly why everybody was going there.

36
00:01:53,355 --> 00:01:55,048
The entrance was a funnel.

37
00:01:55,398 --> 00:01:59,642
Hundreds of people pushing through two doors, and the noise bouncing off the glass.

38
00:01:59,992 --> 00:02:01,880
I told myself it was fine.

39
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:03,649
Crowds mean help.

40
00:02:03,999 --> 00:02:06,069
Crowds mean someone is in charge.

41
00:02:06,969 --> 00:02:08,753
Inside, it got worse.

42
00:02:09,103 --> 00:02:12,644
A man shouted for everyone to stay calm, and nobody listened.

43
00:02:12,994 --> 00:02:15,338
A child was crying somewhere above me.

44
00:02:15,688 --> 00:02:19,763
I found a small kiosk with its shutter half open and took what I could carry.

45
00:02:20,113 --> 00:02:21,688
Two bottles of water.

46
00:02:22,038 --> 00:02:23,575
Three cans of food.

47
00:02:23,925 --> 00:02:26,060
I felt almost proud of myself.

48
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:28,704
I did not look for exits.

49
00:02:29,054 --> 00:02:31,203
I did not even think about exits.

50
00:02:31,553 --> 00:02:33,427
I did what everyone else did.

51
00:02:33,777 --> 00:02:37,045
I followed the noise, and I told myself that was a plan.

52
00:02:37,945 --> 00:02:39,898
It started on the upper level.

53
00:02:40,248 --> 00:02:41,550
I never saw how.

54
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:47,994
First a scream, then a surge, and then the whole floor was moving at once toward the only place anyone could think of.

55
00:02:48,344 --> 00:02:49,489
The stairwell.

56
00:02:50,389 --> 00:02:51,704
I got swept in.

57
00:02:52,054 --> 00:02:55,140
The stairs were too narrow for the number of people on them.

58
00:02:55,490 --> 00:02:59,786
Shoulders, elbows, bags, and a metal handrail running down the middle.

59
00:03:00,136 --> 00:03:01,803
My backpack caught on it.

60
00:03:02,703 --> 00:03:05,919
For a moment I did not understand why I had stopped moving.

61
00:03:06,269 --> 00:03:10,188
The crowd kept pushing, and the strap held me to the railing like a hand.

62
00:03:10,538 --> 00:03:11,827
I pulled once.

63
00:03:12,177 --> 00:03:12,997
Nothing.

64
00:03:13,347 --> 00:03:15,287
People were shouting behind me.

65
00:03:15,637 --> 00:03:16,965
Someone fell.

66
00:03:17,315 --> 00:03:20,843
Below us the sound changed, and I knew what it meant without looking.

67
00:03:21,743 --> 00:03:26,847
I slipped one arm out of the strap, dragged the bag free, and tore my palm open on the metal.

68
00:03:27,197 --> 00:03:28,199
It stung.

69
00:03:28,549 --> 00:03:29,903
I did not care.

70
00:03:30,803 --> 00:03:34,214
At the next landing there was a grey door with three words on it.

71
00:03:34,564 --> 00:03:35,775
Staff only.

72
00:03:36,675 --> 00:03:38,029
I did not choose it.

73
00:03:38,379 --> 00:03:40,579
I was pushed toward it, and it opened.

74
00:03:40,929 --> 00:03:44,158
A corridor, cold air, the smell of cleaning fluid.

75
00:03:44,508 --> 00:03:46,644
Through the wall I could hear the mall.

76
00:03:46,994 --> 00:03:53,204
I ran the other way, down a ramp, through a second door, and out onto a loading dock where the morning was suddenly quiet.

77
00:03:54,104 --> 00:03:58,271
I sat down between two dumpsters, and I realised my hand was shaking.

78
00:03:59,171 --> 00:04:03,103
I did not know what to do, so I did what I always do when I am scared.

79
00:04:03,453 --> 00:04:04,677
I made a list.

80
00:04:05,577 --> 00:04:11,123
I opened the notes on my phone and typed with one thumb, because my other hand was bleeding onto my sleeve.

81
00:04:11,473 --> 00:04:13,153
I did not call it rules.

82
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:15,495
I did not know enough for rules.

83
00:04:15,845 --> 00:04:18,605
I wrote down only what I had seen with my own eyes.

84
00:04:19,505 --> 00:04:20,208
One.

85
00:04:20,558 --> 00:04:22,602
The ones from the mall did not run.

86
00:04:22,952 --> 00:04:23,902
They walked.

87
00:04:24,802 --> 00:04:25,505
Two.

88
00:04:25,855 --> 00:04:27,495
The crowd made them come.

89
00:04:27,845 --> 00:04:30,202
Every scream seemed to pull them closer.

90
00:04:31,102 --> 00:04:32,000
Three.

91
00:04:32,350 --> 00:04:34,394
I do not know how many there are.

92
00:04:35,294 --> 00:04:37,794
Two percent of my battery for three lines.

93
00:04:38,144 --> 00:04:39,641
It felt like a waste.

94
00:04:39,991 --> 00:04:42,764
It was the first useful thing I had done all day.

95
00:04:43,664 --> 00:04:46,932
From behind the dumpster I could see a long stretch of street.

96
00:04:47,282 --> 00:04:53,701
Somewhere in the mall an alarm was ringing and ringing, and the people left out here were drifting toward it, one after another.

97
00:04:54,051 --> 00:04:55,640
They did not look for me.

98
00:04:55,990 --> 00:04:57,291
They did not run.

99
00:04:57,641 --> 00:05:00,831
They walked toward the sound the way water finds a low place.

100
00:05:01,731 --> 00:05:05,611
I watched them for a long time, and I did not yet know what I was watching.

101
00:05:06,511 --> 00:05:10,157
By the afternoon I needed somewhere to rest, and I wanted a bed.

102
00:05:10,507 --> 00:05:14,686
The streets had gone quiet the way a place does when everyone has left in a hurry.

103
00:05:15,036 --> 00:05:17,224
At the end of a row I found a house.

104
00:05:17,574 --> 00:05:19,995
The front door stood open a hand's width.

105
00:05:20,345 --> 00:05:21,387
No lights.

106
00:05:21,737 --> 00:05:23,455
It looked like what I wanted.

107
00:05:24,355 --> 00:05:27,285
I pushed the door and called out, softly, hello?

108
00:05:27,635 --> 00:05:29,744
I think I wanted someone to answer.

109
00:05:30,094 --> 00:05:31,435
Nobody answered.

110
00:05:32,335 --> 00:05:33,819
Then I saw the frame.

111
00:05:34,169 --> 00:05:38,387
The wood around the lock was splintered, and the splinters pointed out, not in.

112
00:05:38,737 --> 00:05:41,068
Whatever broke that door had been inside.

113
00:05:41,968 --> 00:05:43,726
Something moved upstairs.

114
00:05:44,076 --> 00:05:48,242
A slow step, then another, then the sound of something dragging along a wall.

115
00:05:48,592 --> 00:05:52,798
I stood in the hall with my heart pounding in my ears, and I still did not run.

116
00:05:53,148 --> 00:05:56,155
I did not know what a running person sounds like to them.

117
00:05:57,055 --> 00:05:59,164
The steps started down the stairs.

118
00:05:59,514 --> 00:06:00,634
Then I ran.

119
00:06:00,984 --> 00:06:09,747
I hit the front door with my shoulder, knocked a vase off a table, and I did not stop until I was three streets away, bent over a garden wall, listening to my own breath.

120
00:06:10,647 --> 00:06:12,521
Nothing had followed me far.

121
00:06:12,871 --> 00:06:16,738
It had stopped at the door, the way a dog stops at the edge of the garden.

122
00:06:17,088 --> 00:06:19,015
I do not think it was clever.

123
00:06:19,365 --> 00:06:23,037
I think it had simply lost interest the moment I stopped making noise.

124
00:06:23,937 --> 00:06:27,999
I thought about that for a long time, because I could not stop thinking about it.

125
00:06:28,899 --> 00:06:30,995
The light was already going orange.

126
00:06:31,345 --> 00:06:34,548
I had no plan, only a body that wanted to stop.

127
00:06:34,898 --> 00:06:38,570
I tried a parking garage first, but the gate was shut and chained.

128
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:45,482
I tried an apartment block, but the stairwell smelled of smoke, and I turned back at the first landing, remembering the mall.

129
00:06:46,382 --> 00:06:51,278
I was near the end of the street when I saw a small utility building behind a row of shops.

130
00:06:51,628 --> 00:06:53,555
One steel door at the front.

131
00:06:53,905 --> 00:06:55,571
A narrow hatch at the back.

132
00:06:55,921 --> 00:06:57,119
No windows.

133
00:06:57,469 --> 00:06:59,747
It was cold, and it smelled of oil.

134
00:07:00,097 --> 00:07:04,394
It had no water, no bed, nothing a normal person would call comfortable.

135
00:07:05,294 --> 00:07:07,637
I do not want to pretend that I chose it.

136
00:07:07,987 --> 00:07:09,810
It was the last place left.

137
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:12,608
I tried the handle, and it was not locked.

138
00:07:13,508 --> 00:07:16,190
I went in, and I closed the door behind me.

139
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:19,821
For the first time since the alert, nobody was running.

140
00:07:20,721 --> 00:07:22,114
Night came fast.

141
00:07:22,464 --> 00:07:25,550
With the power gone, the city went completely dark.

142
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:29,858
I was afraid of the dark, so I switched on the flashlight and I left it on.

143
00:07:30,208 --> 00:07:34,973
I sat in the middle of the room with the beam on the door, as if the light could keep it shut.

144
00:07:35,873 --> 00:07:37,618
Around midnight I heard it.

145
00:07:37,968 --> 00:07:39,348
A scrape outside.

146
00:07:39,698 --> 00:07:40,791
Then another.

147
00:07:41,141 --> 00:07:43,641
Something dragging a foot across concrete.

148
00:07:44,541 --> 00:07:46,025
The steel door moved.

149
00:07:46,375 --> 00:07:47,469
Not a knock.

150
00:07:47,819 --> 00:07:48,782
A push.

151
00:07:49,132 --> 00:07:49,991
Once.

152
00:07:50,341 --> 00:07:51,148
Twice.

153
00:07:51,498 --> 00:07:53,842
Then a slow rhythm of hands on metal.

154
00:07:54,192 --> 00:07:55,389
More hands.

155
00:07:55,739 --> 00:07:57,354
I could hear them gathering.

156
00:07:57,704 --> 00:08:04,357
I thought of the street at the mall, of the people drifting toward the alarm, and I understood with a horrible clarity what I had done.

157
00:08:04,707 --> 00:08:07,155
I had switched on a light in a black city.

158
00:08:07,505 --> 00:08:09,549
I had made myself the alarm.

159
00:08:10,449 --> 00:08:15,136
My hand was shaking so hard that the flashlight slipped and rolled across the floor and went out.

160
00:08:16,036 --> 00:08:17,676
The darkness was total.

161
00:08:18,026 --> 00:08:19,354
I held my breath.

162
00:08:19,704 --> 00:08:21,866
I pressed myself against the wall.

163
00:08:22,216 --> 00:08:26,278
The pushing went on for a while, and then, little by little, it thinned.

164
00:08:26,628 --> 00:08:27,839
A last scrape.

165
00:08:28,189 --> 00:08:29,295
Then nothing.

166
00:08:29,645 --> 00:08:31,663
I do not know how long I waited.

167
00:08:32,013 --> 00:08:36,075
When I finally breathed out, it felt as if I had been holding it for an hour.

168
00:08:36,975 --> 00:08:39,097
They had stopped because I had stopped.

169
00:08:39,447 --> 00:08:45,033
The light was gone, the noise was gone, and in a few minutes they had forgotten there was anything here at all.

170
00:08:45,933 --> 00:08:48,225
I did not turn the flashlight on again.

171
00:08:48,575 --> 00:08:54,160
I stayed on my knees against the wall until it was light, and I told myself, over and over, one word.

172
00:08:54,510 --> 00:08:55,330
Quiet.

173
00:08:56,230 --> 00:08:57,819
Dawn came grey and slow.

174
00:08:58,169 --> 00:09:02,622
I opened the hatch a finger's width, looked at an empty yard, and closed it again.

175
00:09:02,972 --> 00:09:05,510
I had been awake for more than twenty hours.

176
00:09:05,860 --> 00:09:13,451
I had a little over a litre of water, three meals of food, a scraped hand, a phone at seventy percent, and a flashlight I was afraid to touch.

177
00:09:14,351 --> 00:09:17,567
I took out the phone and added a fourth line under my three.

178
00:09:17,917 --> 00:09:20,235
It was not a list of things I had seen.

179
00:09:20,585 --> 00:09:22,668
It was the first thing I had learned.

180
00:09:23,018 --> 00:09:24,333
They come to noise.

181
00:09:24,683 --> 00:09:25,985
So be quiet.

182
00:09:26,885 --> 00:09:28,395
Then the phone buzzed.

183
00:09:28,745 --> 00:09:29,903
A new message.

184
00:09:30,253 --> 00:09:31,295
Automated.

185
00:09:31,645 --> 00:09:32,517
Flat.

186
00:09:32,867 --> 00:09:34,377
Evacuation point.

187
00:09:34,727 --> 00:09:37,097
River Crossing Bridge, north bank.

188
00:09:37,447 --> 00:09:39,335
Cut-off, twelve noon today.

189
00:09:40,235 --> 00:09:41,784
I read it four times.

190
00:09:42,134 --> 00:09:44,178
I should have asked who was sending it.

191
00:09:44,528 --> 00:09:47,275
I should have asked how many other people had read it.

192
00:09:47,625 --> 00:09:50,229
Instead I did what a tired person does.

193
00:09:50,579 --> 00:09:52,232
I wanted it to be true.

194
00:09:53,132 --> 00:09:54,994
I counted my supplies again.

195
00:09:55,344 --> 00:10:00,201
I put on the backpack, I stepped out into the cold, and I started walking toward the river.

196
00:10:00,551 --> 00:10:05,160
For the first time since the alert, I walked slowly, and I tried not to make a sound.
